  "fixture_id": "polynetwork_2021",
  "notes": "Root cause (Poly Network, Aug 2021): EthCrossChainManager.verifyHeaderAndExecuteTx placed no restriction on which contract/method a cross-chain message could invoke. Because ECCM owns EthCrossChainData (ECCD), a message targeting ECCD.putCurEpochConPubKeyBytes (owner-only) replaced the keeper. The honest relay faithfully reports the TRUE source sender, so an attacker cannot forge the fromContract an unlock needs; but once the keeper is the attacker, the attacker submits a header directly and sets fromContract to the registered proxy, draining LockProxy. Keeper modelled as the authorised submitter address; the real function is putCurEpochConPubKeyBytes(bytes) and the real attacker brute-forced a colliding method selector (f1121318093). Patched: forbid messages targeting ECCD (Poly added callable-contract/method whitelists). Sources: SlowMist, BlockSec, Kudelski.",
  "variants": {"vulnerable": "official/vulnerable", "patched": "official/patched"},
  "cross_chain": true,
  "deploy": [
